Critical Database Rules
1. One employee cannot have two active default shifts for the same effective date.

2. One employee cannot have two active roster assignments covering the same date.

3. One employee can have only one employee_duty_roster record per duty_date.

4. One employee can have only one processed attendance_sheet record per duty_date.

5. Raw attendance_logs must never be edited by normal users.

6. attendance_logs must not contain IN/OUT classification.

7. IN/OUT is determined by attendance processing.

8. Cross-midnight shifts use duty_date, not simply calendar date.

9. Attendance sheets cannot be directly edited.

10. Attendance correction must use an application/request.

11. Attendance correction monthly limit is configurable.

12. Approved leave cannot be cancelled by employee.

13. Returned leave can be edited and resubmitted.

14. Leave balance should be auditable through transactions.

15. Leave entitlement is policy-driven.

16. Leave year is independent from payroll period.

17. Payroll period is independent from calendar month.

18. One payroll cycle can be assigned to many employees.

19. An employee can have only one applicable payroll cycle for a particular date.

20. Payroll approval locks the payroll result.

21. Finalized payroll cannot be silently recalculated.

22. Payslip references the finalized payroll.

23. All important changes must be recorded in audit_logs.

24. Historical records should not be deleted casually.

25. Configuration changes should use effective dates wherever historical behavior matters.



